    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, just had a cow come out of rumenotomy this morning. need a solid protocol for the next few days. what should i be looking for regarding infection and how should i handle the diet reintroduction? cheers",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Post-rumenotomy, closely monitor the cow for signs of distress, reduced appetite, abnormal discharge, or fever indicating infection. Keep the wound clean by gently cleaning it daily with chlorhexidine and changing clean bedding. Start with offering small, frequent quantities of highly digestible forage, like grass hay, and delay resumption of concentrate intake to prevent bloating. Gradually increase fiber and grain amounts over 3-5 days, while observing her appetite, manure consistency, and overall behavior for any adverse reactions. Ensure she is progressively returning to her regular ruminating sounds and activity level, and consult your veterinarian if necessary.",
      "source": "target",
